WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.368 --> 00:00:02.951
(spooky music)

00:00:04.498 --> 00:00:06.310
(haunting music)

00:00:06.310 --> 00:00:09.050
- [David] I've heard of a
border crossing experience

00:00:09.050 --> 00:00:11.120
that turns being an illegal migrant

00:00:11.120 --> 00:00:13.560
into a tourist attraction.

00:00:13.560 --> 00:00:17.030
I want to find out what making
that journey would be like.

00:00:17.030 --> 00:00:19.513
And how realistic this tour is.

00:00:20.450 --> 00:00:23.060
President Trump campaigned
to build a wall,

00:00:23.060 --> 00:00:26.290
so I'm surprised there's already one here.

00:00:26.290 --> 00:00:28.260
It's more like a fence than a wall.

00:00:28.260 --> 00:00:30.030
And it's not even finished.

00:00:30.030 --> 00:00:32.600
Surely this tour is
going to be pretty easy.

00:00:32.600 --> 00:00:35.970
Our commander takes his
role very seriously,

00:00:35.970 --> 00:00:38.060
and we nervously set off.

00:00:38.060 --> 00:00:41.145
The action starts almost as
soon as our six hour trek

00:00:41.145 --> 00:00:42.664
to the pretend border begins.

00:00:42.664 --> 00:00:43.497
(gunshot)

00:00:43.497 --> 00:00:44.330
- [Man] Whoa! Shit!

00:00:44.330 --> 00:00:46.830
- [David] I don't know
where they're coming from,

00:00:46.830 --> 00:00:48.766
but those gunshots sounded very authentic.

00:00:48.766 --> 00:00:50.120
(panicked Spanish)

00:00:50.120 --> 00:00:51.920
How real is this going to get?

00:00:51.920 --> 00:00:53.444
Well that's the thing I don't know

00:00:53.444 --> 00:00:54.277
if it's just Mexico or the tour.

00:00:54.277 --> 00:00:56.020
I'm jittery with nerves,

00:00:56.020 --> 00:00:57.844
and I don't know what's going on.

00:00:57.844 --> 00:00:58.910
(gunshots)

00:00:58.910 --> 00:01:00.080
Who is shooting at us?

00:01:00.080 --> 00:01:01.789
We're about to find out.

00:01:01.789 --> 00:01:03.028
(gunshots)
(woman screams)

00:01:03.028 --> 00:01:05.778
(urgent yelling)

00:01:06.830 --> 00:01:08.980
Apparently being robbed by criminals

00:01:08.980 --> 00:01:11.165
on your way to the border is common.

00:01:11.165 --> 00:01:12.380
(Robbers yelling in Spanish)

00:01:12.380 --> 00:01:14.950
For a split second I
forget this is a tour.

00:01:14.950 --> 00:01:16.627
Quite authentic.

00:01:16.627 --> 00:01:18.840
(Robbers yelling in Spanish)

00:01:18.840 --> 00:01:20.820
I look to our commander for guidance.

00:01:20.820 --> 00:01:22.110
Commander, what's going on?

00:01:22.110 --> 00:01:23.860
But I should've kept my mouth shut.

00:01:25.034 --> 00:01:27.030
(Spanish yelling)

00:01:27.030 --> 00:01:28.374
You can take that.

00:01:28.374 --> 00:01:29.601
Oh!
(thuds)

00:01:29.601 --> 00:01:31.320
(Spanish yelling)

00:01:31.320 --> 00:01:33.570
I don't really know how to react.

00:01:33.570 --> 00:01:35.481
This just seems nuts.

00:01:35.481 --> 00:01:36.314
(Spanish speaking)

00:01:36.314 --> 00:01:37.913
I only know English. No Spanish.

00:01:37.913 --> 00:01:41.928
It's a weird mix of amateur
drama and violent reality.

00:01:41.928 --> 00:01:42.761
(soaring)

00:01:42.761 --> 00:01:45.800
Until now this has been a restricted area,

00:01:45.800 --> 00:01:47.850
but the government says it's now okay

00:01:47.850 --> 00:01:49.453
for residents to return.

00:01:50.810 --> 00:01:52.700
I had to come and see for myself

00:01:52.700 --> 00:01:54.603
what a nuclear disaster looks like.

00:01:55.600 --> 00:01:57.173
Is it safe to be here?

00:01:58.270 --> 00:02:01.430
- [Yow] So ladies and gentlemen
I'm your tourist guide.

00:02:01.430 --> 00:02:03.530
- [David] Our guide for the day is Yow.

00:02:03.530 --> 00:02:06.380
So I have to be careful
with my right and left

00:02:06.380 --> 00:02:08.053
because to you it's switched.

00:02:09.260 --> 00:02:13.416
So I have to say, "On your
right" and "On your left".

00:02:13.416 --> 00:02:14.650
(laughs)

00:02:14.650 --> 00:02:16.500
- [David] It seems like just another walk

00:02:16.500 --> 00:02:18.900
in the radioactive park for Yow.

00:02:18.900 --> 00:02:21.623
He certainly doesn't seem
concerned about any danger.

00:02:21.623 --> 00:02:22.490
(meter beeping)

00:02:22.490 --> 00:02:25.550
What are the levels that
you'd be concerned about, Yow?

00:02:25.550 --> 00:02:29.315
So for livin' in the area point two zero.

00:02:29.315 --> 00:02:30.148
(beeping)

00:02:30.148 --> 00:02:31.460
Worries me.

00:02:31.460 --> 00:02:32.410
- [David] Okay.

00:02:32.410 --> 00:02:33.810
It's funny, because it's very hard

00:02:33.810 --> 00:02:35.890
because you are such a happy person

00:02:35.890 --> 00:02:38.450
it's very hard to know, for me,

00:02:38.450 --> 00:02:41.028
and for us, how dangerous it is.

00:02:41.028 --> 00:02:44.276
- [Yow] I'm not growing
extra horns or extra fingers.

00:02:44.276 --> 00:02:45.109
(steady beeping)

00:02:45.109 --> 00:02:46.150
- [David] One point nine

00:02:46.150 --> 00:02:47.467
- [Woman 1] Two point three

00:02:47.467 --> 00:02:49.089
Two point eight

00:02:49.089 --> 00:02:50.830
(beeping increases)

00:02:50.830 --> 00:02:53.020
The levels keep rising.

00:02:53.020 --> 00:02:55.768
Everyone is seriously on edge.

00:02:55.768 --> 00:02:57.430
(chirping beeps)

00:02:57.430 --> 00:02:59.970
No one was expecting readings this high.

00:02:59.970 --> 00:03:01.463
Not even our own crew.

00:03:03.033 --> 00:03:06.479
So what we just experienced
was even the highest.

00:03:06.479 --> 00:03:07.528
No.

00:03:07.528 --> 00:03:08.955
So that wasn't the hot spot.

00:03:08.955 --> 00:03:10.386
No.

00:03:10.386 --> 00:03:11.219
You know that.

00:03:11.219 --> 00:03:12.690
Well I'm probably gonna stay on the bus.

00:03:12.690 --> 00:03:14.120
- [David] Even the bus doesn't feel

00:03:14.120 --> 00:03:15.770
like it a shield anymore.

00:03:15.770 --> 00:03:18.460
And the levels continue to get higher.

00:03:18.460 --> 00:03:19.577
- [Woman 1] Oh my god!

00:03:19.577 --> 00:03:20.410
- [Woman 2] One point eight seven

00:03:20.410 --> 00:03:21.243
(gasping)
- [Woman 1] Oh my god!

00:03:21.243 --> 00:03:22.076
(panicked talking)

00:03:22.076 --> 00:03:23.722
(meter beeping increasing)

00:03:23.722 --> 00:03:24.810
Guys, seven point one nine.

00:03:24.810 --> 00:03:25.643
- [Woman 2] Oh my God!

00:03:25.643 --> 00:03:27.980
- [David] The readings are
now about 50 times over

00:03:27.980 --> 00:03:30.590
the zero point two threshold.

00:03:30.590 --> 00:03:33.020
I don't want to stay another minute here,

00:03:33.020 --> 00:03:33.980
and I'm not alone.

00:03:33.980 --> 00:03:35.531
- [Woman 1] I have nine
point seven one now.

00:03:35.531 --> 00:03:36.670
Scare point.

00:03:36.670 --> 00:03:37.622
- [Woman 1] Alright.

00:03:37.622 --> 00:03:39.240
- [Woman 2] We're scared.
- [Male] We are scared, okay.

00:03:39.240 --> 00:03:40.745
- [Woman 1] We have
officially been scared.

00:03:40.745 --> 00:03:41.578
- [David] Yeah.

00:03:41.578 --> 00:03:42.411
- [Woman 1] Let's go back.

00:03:42.411 --> 00:03:43.244
- [Woman 2] He's say let's go

00:03:43.244 --> 00:03:44.077
- [Woman 1] All in favor?

00:03:44.077 --> 00:03:44.910
Okay.

00:03:44.910 --> 00:03:45.780
(Passengers agreeing)

00:03:45.780 --> 00:03:46.613
Who wants to go?

00:03:46.613 --> 00:03:49.459
(Passengers murmuring agreement)

00:03:49.459 --> 00:03:50.292
(engine sputters)

00:03:50.292 --> 00:03:51.125
(chuckles)

00:03:51.125 --> 00:03:53.256
The driver just turned off the engine.

00:03:53.256 --> 00:03:54.432
(meter beeping rapidly)

00:03:54.432 --> 00:03:55.493
(passengers talking)

00:03:55.493 --> 00:03:57.174
Not the place to breakdown.

00:03:57.174 --> 00:03:58.399
(soaring)
Twenty

00:03:58.399 --> 00:03:59.760
and five.

00:03:59.760 --> 00:04:02.194
Alright so let me get you guys wristbands.

00:04:02.194 --> 00:04:03.241
(crowd chattering)

00:04:03.241 --> 00:04:05.280
Alright everybody that is coming

00:04:05.280 --> 00:04:08.100
on the Cream City
Cannibal Tour this evening

00:04:08.100 --> 00:04:11.280
could you please join us
outside in the alleyway,

00:04:11.280 --> 00:04:13.054
so we may begin this tour.

00:04:13.054 --> 00:04:14.490
(crowd talking)

00:04:14.490 --> 00:04:18.210
- [David] Natalie was spot on
about Bachelorette parties.

00:04:18.210 --> 00:04:21.594
The tour is dominated by
women in their thirties.

00:04:21.594 --> 00:04:23.531
Maybe, like the tour guides

00:04:23.531 --> 00:04:26.630
they're all secretly
hot for Jeffry Dahmer.

00:04:26.630 --> 00:04:28.123
The ultimate bad boy.

00:04:29.500 --> 00:04:32.910
I'm just excited to finally
satisfy my bloody curiosity

00:04:32.910 --> 00:04:34.937
by getting into the graphic details.

00:04:34.937 --> 00:04:36.800
[Female Tour Guide]
Another method he used is

00:04:36.800 --> 00:04:39.200
he actually tried to create a sex slave

00:04:39.200 --> 00:04:40.700
that wouldn't have any needs.

00:04:40.700 --> 00:04:41.533
Wouldn't speak.

00:04:41.533 --> 00:04:42.860
Wouldn't do much.

00:04:42.860 --> 00:04:44.480
But he still wanted them alive,

00:04:44.480 --> 00:04:46.630
so to do this he decided to drill

00:04:46.630 --> 00:04:50.200
an inch and a quarter into their skulls,

00:04:50.200 --> 00:04:53.830
and at first he poured boiling water,

00:04:53.830 --> 00:04:57.200
and then he tried
different cleaning agents.

00:04:57.200 --> 00:04:59.530
- [David] I'm into all
these disgusting bits,

00:04:59.530 --> 00:05:00.520
and I'm not the only one.

00:05:00.520 --> 00:05:02.330
He's super interesting. Yes.

00:05:02.330 --> 00:05:05.150
'Cause he's very different
than the stereotypical.

00:05:05.150 --> 00:05:07.090
But I think women also just
want to fix everybody too.

00:05:07.090 --> 00:05:08.180
I don't think that's

00:05:08.180 --> 00:05:09.200
Oh, way to be psychological.

00:05:09.200 --> 00:05:10.033
I know.

00:05:10.033 --> 00:05:10.866
Well it's true.
Yeah, you tell them Lorna.

00:05:10.866 --> 00:05:12.283
I mean. Yeah.

00:05:13.140 --> 00:05:14.239
- [David] How would you affect him?

00:05:14.239 --> 00:05:15.589
What would be your methodology?

00:05:15.589 --> 00:05:16.422
(women laughing)

00:05:16.422 --> 00:05:17.823
Li'l snuggles.
(laughs)

00:05:17.823 --> 00:05:20.035
A li'l drill in the brain.

00:05:20.035 --> 00:05:20.868
(laughing)

00:05:20.868 --> 00:05:22.169
Snuggles, but not too close.

00:05:22.169 --> 00:05:23.060
(laughs)

00:05:23.060 --> 00:05:25.410
- [David] The tour takes us to Club 219

00:05:25.410 --> 00:05:28.053
where Dahmer picked up
many of his victims.

00:05:29.030 --> 00:05:30.910
And things start to get weird.

00:05:30.910 --> 00:05:32.620
If anyone is here with us right now

00:05:32.620 --> 00:05:34.133
Can you please cross the rods?

00:05:37.100 --> 00:05:39.050
- [Woman] That's a yes.

00:05:39.050 --> 00:05:41.543
Now can you please
uncross the rods for me?

00:05:43.500 --> 00:05:44.980
If you're feeling low on energy

00:05:44.980 --> 00:05:47.223
you may use my energy if need be.

00:05:48.730 --> 00:05:51.510
If we are speaking to
Jeffry Dahmer currently

00:05:51.510 --> 00:05:53.713
can you please cross the rods?

00:05:58.250 --> 00:06:00.370
Does anybody have any
questions for Mr. Dahmer?

00:06:00.370 --> 00:06:02.376
That lost me Natalie.

00:06:02.376 --> 00:06:04.000
Have they lost you?

00:06:04.000 --> 00:06:04.833
Totally.
(soaring)

00:06:04.833 --> 00:06:06.730
- [David] I've decided
to get out of Ashgabat

00:06:06.730 --> 00:06:08.240
and its tight security.

00:06:08.240 --> 00:06:11.683
To see if things are more
relaxed outside the city walls.

00:06:14.190 --> 00:06:16.010
And what better excuse than going

00:06:16.010 --> 00:06:18.073
to a famed tourist destination?

00:06:19.040 --> 00:06:23.000
The Gates of Hell is a
spectacular flaming pit.

00:06:23.000 --> 00:06:25.660
It's the result of a Soviet
oil drilling accident

00:06:25.660 --> 00:06:26.969
that was meant to be extinguished

00:06:26.969 --> 00:06:29.510
by setting fire to the oil.

00:06:29.510 --> 00:06:33.090
But 40 years later it's still burning.

00:06:33.090 --> 00:06:35.600
But our plans come to a grinding halt

00:06:35.600 --> 00:06:37.070
when we board the tour bus.

00:06:37.070 --> 00:06:38.505
- [Male Friend] That would
be a bit of a problem. Yeah.

00:06:38.505 --> 00:06:40.554
I spoke to my manager and I asked

00:06:40.554 --> 00:06:42.810
[David} We're informed the
President has closed off

00:06:42.810 --> 00:06:46.530
the entire city of
Ashgabat from the country.

00:06:46.530 --> 00:06:48.563
And journalists are not allowed out.

00:06:50.720 --> 00:06:53.430
As a consolation officials offer us a tour

00:06:53.430 --> 00:06:54.870
of the inner city.

00:06:54.870 --> 00:06:57.830
A chance to see some of the
President's prized memorials

00:06:57.830 --> 00:06:59.210
and statues.

00:06:59.210 --> 00:07:01.810
- [Driver] Yeah you can
take video but without

00:07:01.810 --> 00:07:02.643
Without you in it.

00:07:02.643 --> 00:07:03.950
- [Driver] Yeah exactly.

00:07:03.950 --> 00:07:05.690
- [David] It turns out
we're not even allowed

00:07:05.690 --> 00:07:07.240
to film any locals.

00:07:07.240 --> 00:07:08.751
Including our driver.

00:07:08.751 --> 00:07:11.228
- [Driver] You can take video of places.

00:07:11.228 --> 00:07:13.104
- [Male Friend] All of the
buildings here are so impressive.

00:07:13.104 --> 00:07:14.404
- [Driver] Many of our new buildings

00:07:14.404 --> 00:07:15.560
we make with white marble.

00:07:15.560 --> 00:07:17.390
- [Male Friend] White marble.
- [Driver] Yes.

00:07:17.390 --> 00:07:19.930
- [David] As well as love for white marble

00:07:19.930 --> 00:07:22.350
the President has a child-like obsession

00:07:22.350 --> 00:07:24.840
with collecting Guinness World Records.

00:07:24.840 --> 00:07:27.044
And surprisingly Ashgabat holds the record

00:07:27.044 --> 00:07:31.260
for Highest Density of Buildings
with White Marble Cladding.

00:07:31.260 --> 00:07:32.700
- [Driver] That was the TV building

00:07:32.700 --> 00:07:33.533
TV building?

00:07:33.533 --> 00:07:36.730
- [Driver] It was also,
uh, third Guinness Record.

00:07:36.730 --> 00:07:38.570
- [David] This tower won a World Record

00:07:38.570 --> 00:07:41.796
for Largest Architectural Image of a Star.

00:07:41.796 --> 00:07:43.064
- [Male Friend] It's ridiculous.

00:07:43.064 --> 00:07:43.897
What is it?

00:07:43.897 --> 00:07:46.057
- [Driver] Like London
Eye our Turkman Eye.

00:07:46.057 --> 00:07:47.700
- [David] And again a Guinness Record

00:07:47.700 --> 00:07:49.410
for the highly contested title

00:07:49.410 --> 00:07:52.150
of World's Largest Indoor Ferris Wheel.

00:07:52.150 --> 00:07:55.572
Was all this stuff built for
the people that live here, or?

00:07:55.572 --> 00:07:57.075
Why's all this,

00:07:57.075 --> 00:07:58.930
oh my God

00:07:58.930 --> 00:08:01.083
Why is all this stuff built even?

00:08:01.083 --> 00:08:03.666
(cymbal clang)

